  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given a tree with NNN vertices.\n\nInitialize a variable X=0X = 0X=0. You would like to perform the following operation N−1N-1N−1 times:\n\n\nChoose an edge (u,v)(u,v)(u,v) that still hasn't been deleted.\nDelete the edge (u,v)(u,v)(u,v).\nLet siz(u)\\text{siz}(u)siz(u) denote the size of the connected component that uuu is contained in and siz(v)\\text{siz}(v)siz(v) denote the size of the connected component that vvv is contained in. XOR the variable XXX with either siz(u)\\text{siz}(u)siz(u) or siz(v)\\text{siz}(v)siz(v). More formally, do any **one** of the following 222 operations:\n\nX=X⊕siz(u)X = X \\oplus \\text{siz}(u)X=X⊕siz(u)\nX=X⊕siz(v)X = X \\oplus \\text{siz}(v)X=X⊕siz(v)\n\n\nFind the **minimum** possible value of XXX that can be achieved after performing all N−1N-1N−1 operations.\n\nAdditionally, provide a valid sequence of operations that achieves this minimum value of XXX. If there are multiple sequences of operations that achieve the minimum value of XXX, you may output any of them.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of multiple lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains an integer NNN — the number of vertices of the tree.\nThe next N−1N-1N−1 lines describe the edges. The iii-th of these N−1N-1N−1 lines contains two space-separated integers uiu_iui​ and viv_ivi​, denoting an edge between uiu_iui​ and viv_ivi​.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output NNN lines.\n\n\n\nOn the first line, print the minimum possible value of XXX.\nOn the iii-th of the next N−1N-1N−1 lines, output three space-separated integers uiu_iui​, viv_ivi​, xix_ixi​, where one of xi=uix_i = u_ixi​=ui​ or xi=vix_i = v_ixi​=vi​ holds - denoting that the edge (ui,vi)(u_i,v_i)(ui​,vi​) is deleted on the iii-th operation, after which XXX is set to X⊕siz(xi)X \\oplus \\text{siz}(x_i)X⊕siz(xi​).\n\nIf there are multiple sequences of operations that minimize XXX, you may output any of them.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1051 \\leq T \\leq 10^51≤T≤105",
      "2≤N≤2⋅1052 \\leq N \\leq 2\\cdot 10^52≤N≤2⋅105",
      "1≤ui,vi≤N1 \\leq u_i, v_i \\leq N1≤ui​,vi​≤N",
      "The input graph describes a tree.",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 2⋅1052\\cdot 10^52⋅105."
    ],
